# Inventory and secrets

Adding a **NixOS** host requires all of: `Makefile` lists,
`config/fleet-inventory.nix`, `hosts/<name>/`, `secrets/<name>/secrets.yaml`,
`ssh/fleet_known_hosts`, flake `nixosConfigurations`. Then
`make check-inventory` and `make edit-secrets HOST=<name>` /
`make updatekeys`.

Ansible Debian guests use inventory MagicDNS paths under `secrets/`
(`proxmox-applications-debian`, `proxmox-gitlab-debian`,
`proxmox-observability-debian`) encrypted to **alex only**. Builder stays
`secrets/proxmox-dev/`. ADR:
[docs/adr/2026-11-06-ansible-guest-secrets.md](../../docs/adr/2026-11-06-ansible-guest-secrets.md).

The two host lists are allowed to exist; they must not drift
(`docs/adr/2026-08-29-inventory-check.md`). `DEPLOY_PAUSED` must match
`fleet.inventory.deployPausedHosts`. CI runs `check-inventory` and
`check-secrets-keys` in `test`. `make check-secrets` is local (age key
decrypt); CI checks required key *names* without decrypting.

Per-host sops files. No shared secret file. Creation rules in `.sops.yaml`
map each `secrets/<host>/` to the right recipients (NixOS: alex + host age;
Ansible guests: alex only; router: alex + proxmox-dev-debian SSH age).
